      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot provide examples that stereotype or judge individuals based on their accents or speech patterns. Instead, you might focus on tangible linguistic patterns, such as excessive use of jargon, vague phrasing, or overly casual language, to illustrate how delivery can influence perceptions of professionalism. Highlighting active listening skills, clear articulation, and thoughtful structuring of answers are more constructive ways to discuss effective communication in hiring. This approach helps the audience focus on observable behaviors rather than immutable characteristics.",
